<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="#">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/power-management">Power Management</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">IGBT &amp; SiC Power Modules</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">Power Management products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s active" href="/markets/power-management/igbt-sic-modules"><span class="abbr">IS</span><span class="label">IGBT &amp; SiC Power Modules</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/power-management/power-discrete"><span class="abbr">PD</span><span class="label">Power Discrete Assembly</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us the device, the current and the package and we&rsquo;ll point you to the right line.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Power Management &middot; IGBT &amp; SiC Power Modules</div><h1 class="mk-h1">IGBT and SiC power module assembly and test</h1><p class="mk-lede">Hana manufactures IGBT and SiC power modules using multi-die assembly on ceramic substrates, with controlled die attach, substrate and baseplate joints, and heavy-current interconnect. These processes form the electrical and thermal paths that determine module performance under repeated switching and thermal cycling.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#specialize-igbt-sic-modules" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;height:420px;border-bottom:0;"><div style="position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px;width:18px;height:18px;opacity:.4;z-index:1;"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"></path></svg></div><span class="cap">[ IGBT &amp; SiC Power Modules &mdash; photography needed ]</span></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-igbt-sic-modules" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">Hana assembles IGBT and SiC modules and IPMs across standard package families, using multi-die layouts on DBC ceramic, high-thermal die attach, silver-sinter where specified and heavy copper (PCC) interconnect. Power-module manufacturing draws on Hana's wider OSAT and microelectronic-assembly capability in Thailand and China.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet has-media"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">IGBT and SiC power modules</span></div><div class="desc">Multi-die assemblies on DBC ceramic in standard package families: 34 mm and 62 mm, XM3, Econo and Econo Dual3, PIM, HP1, Easy 1B/2B/3B and HEPACK/DBC.</div><div class="pic"><span>[ Photo: IGBT / SiC module on DBC ]</span></div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">Intelligent power modules (IPMs)</span></div><div class="desc">Drive and power stages packaged together as a single module for motor-control programs.</div><div class="pic"><span>[ Photo: Intelligent power module ]</span></div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Compact power packages</span></div><div class="desc">TO-247TE, Top and Dual Cool QFN, INSOP, eeSiP and FC LGA outlines for board-mounted power applications.</div><div class="pic"><span>[ Photo: Compact power package ]</span></div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Reliability and cycling test</span></div><div class="desc">Power cycling, thermal cycling and reliability sequences available according to the program qualification plan.</div><div class="pic"><span>[ Photo: Power cycling test ]</span></div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">See IC Assembly &amp; Test for the die attach, wire and clip bonding, encapsulation and wafer-level processes supporting these packages.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/osat">Explore IC Assembly &amp; Test <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section class="mk-dark"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div style="max-width:820px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark">Die attach, substrate and high-current interconnect</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:0 0 14px;">Power-module assembly requires controlled joints across the die attach, substrate, baseplate and current path. Hana supports solder die attach and silver-sinter where specified, with inspection of the attach layer and heavy copper (PCC) interconnect for high-current designs. Wide-bandgap wafer preparation includes laser grooving followed by blade dicing for SiC, GaN, GaN-on-Si and low-K wafers where required by the material and device construction.</p><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:0 0 14px;">Hana's scope covers the power module itself; integration into the finished inverter, motor drive or charger remains within the customer's system.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">Footprint</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/ayutthaya"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Ayutthaya</div><div class="note">power module assembly, wide-bandgap</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/jiaxing"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">China</span></span><div class="nm">Jiaxing</div><div class="note">IGBT and SiC modules</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What module constructions can Hana assemble?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Hana supports multi-die IGBT and SiC modules and IPMs on DBC ceramic across standard package families including 34 mm, 62 mm, XM3, Econo and Econo Dual3, PIM, HP1, Easy 1B/2B/3B and HEPACK/DBC, together with board-mount outlines such as TO-247TE, Top and Dual Cool QFN, INSOP, eeSiP and FC LGA. Die attach options include solder and silver-sinter, with heavy copper (PCC) interconnect available for high-current designs.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What reliability testing can Hana run on a module?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Power cycling, thermal cycling and reliability sequences are available according to the program qualification plan. The applicable test set is agreed per program and confirmed per site.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How is quality controlled on the thermal path?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Die attach is selected according to the module construction and inspected for voiding, while substrate and baseplate joints are controlled through the manufacturing process. Cycling test can also be applied according to program requirements to verify the completed assembly against its design.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Are these the same as the automotive and industrial power module pages?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">The underlying device and assembly capability is shared across applications. For in-vehicle powertrain programs see <a href="/markets/automotive/power-modules">Automotive power modules</a>; for solar, drives and grid equipment see <a href="/markets/industrial-iot/power-modules">Industrial power modules</a>. This page covers package-level power-module assembly itself.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:40px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/power-management" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Power Management market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your power module program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>